# PROMOTE.manifest -- what publishes from development to the public repo
# ===========================================================================
# Authority chain (single, canonical):
#     D:\code\ccode  (branch: development = source of truth, full history)
#         |  files matched below, minus .gitignore deny-list
#         v
#     C:\x64base     (branch: main = publication staging)
#         |  git commit + push
#         v
#     github.com/deraldg/x64base  (main = public snapshot; canonical for
#                                   downloads and pull requests)
#
# WHAT THIS MANIFEST GOVERNS: the curated DATA + DOCUMENTATION projection that
# publishes to main -- fixtures, the databuild lane, HELP, end-user docs,
# runtime scaffold, launchers. ALLOW-LIST: of the clean dev files, only these
# publish through the rebuild overlay.
#
# WHAT IT ALSO GOVERNS, as of 2026-09-12: engine SOURCE and BUILD CONFIG.
# src/, include/, bindings/, cmake/, config/build_vectors.*, CMakeLists.txt,
# CMakePresets.json and vcpkg*.json are carried HERE, through the one chain
# above. There is no second route and no intermediate curated tree -- which is
# what PROMOTION_PROCESS.md section 2 always said, before it carved out source.
# NEVER merge or push the development branch to main; the overlay copies files,
# not history, which is how it satisfies that rule by construction.
#
# THIS REVERSES THE EARLIER RULE, and it reverses on measurement, not taste.
# The old text said overlaying dev's source "would push half-finished engine
# code to main". That was TRUE while the overlay copied the WORKING TREE. Since
# 651ce911a it copies only what git TRACKS, so uncommitted work cannot travel
# and the hazard is gone. The second reason -- source must be build-coherent,
# presets and CMakeLists and the src/ they configure travelling TOGETHER -- is
# answered by carrying the COMPLETE tracked set (never a subset) and by
# PROMOTION_PROCESS.md section 5 step 3, the staging build, now GATING rather
# than optional. That build is the cold-clone certification.
#
# What the old route bought was curation: publish some committed source, hold
# the rest. Measured 2026-09-12 -- it had not run since 2026-08-09, leaving main
# 71 source files behind with NO src/sqlsel/ AT ALL, while this projection
# published 1.1 manuals describing it. A curation gate nobody runs is worse than
# a sync that always runs.
#
# SCOPE NOTE: this projection is scoped lean for a product-facing main --
# metalevel docs, portal seeds, and doc-engine tools that the promotion model
# would ALLOW here are deliberately trimmed (see NOT PUBLISHED). That is a
# maintainer scope choice on the projection, not a change to the source/git
# boundary above.
#
# FORMAT
#   - '#' begins a comment; blank lines ignored.
#   - Every other line is a path or glob, relative to the development root.
#   - '**' recurses; '**/' matches zero-or-more directory segments;
#     '*' stays within a path segment. Shell globbing.
#   - The rebuild re-applies .gitignore after matching (defense in depth).
# ===========================================================================


# ###########################################################################
# PUBLISHED -- the product (engine + help + samples)
# ###########################################################################

# --- entry + hygiene + license + public-repo health files ------------------
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.github/workflows/*.yml
LICENSE
LICENSING.md
README.md
MANIFEST.txt
BUILDING.md
CHANGELOG.md
RELEASE_NOTES.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md

# --- curated transportable text (AIF-093) ----------------------------------
# `.text` is the opt-in "chosen to travel" marker: any `.text` file, anywhere,
# publishes. Additive -- `.txt` is UNCHANGED and stays governed by its own
# per-path patterns. `**/*.text` globs files (pathlib), not the `dir/**` case.
**/*.text

# --- product launchers -----------------------------------------------------
dottalkpp/bin/*.bat
dottalkpp/bin/*.ps1
dottalkpp/bin/*.sh
dottalkpp/bin/*.ico
# NOTE: main currently carries BUILDING.md at docs/getting-started/BUILDING.md.
# Reconcile to ONE canonical location before the next promotion.

# --- build configuration (travels WITH src/; miss one and the clone fails) --
# Verified against the build graph 2026-09-12: config/build_vectors.cmake is a
# NON-OPTIONAL include at CMakeLists.txt:392 and configure_file consumes the two
# .in templates. GLOBBED, NOT ENUMERATED, and that is the lesson. The first
# attempt listed build_vectors.{cmake,hpp.in,json.in} after grepping for
# configure_file and COUNTING three calls without reading their arguments; the
# third names config/version_stamp.hpp.in (CMakeLists.txt:407) and the staging
# configure died on it. The retry then added a coverage check, which immediately
# found a SECOND miss: tools/packaging/build_product_inventory.py, run by
# execute_process at CONFIGURE time with FATAL_ERROR on nonzero (:723), so a
# clone cannot configure without it either. TWO misses, both by eye, both caught
# mechanically -- which is why the check below is the part that matters, not
# these globs. config/* takes all four templates and any future one;
# config/package/ is untouched (non-recursive) and its three product manifests
# stay listed individually with development.manifest deliberately excluded.
# tools/packaging is not in the NOT PUBLISHED list -- that names manualgen,
# fullstack_docs, gui_preview, ci, hygiene and staging -- it was simply never
# allow-listed because source never travelled. cmake/ is an OPTIONAL
# include (pydottalk). Every CMakeLists.txt in the build graph is reached by
# src/** or bindings/** or the root entry here; tests/ and gui/uidef/ carry
# CMakeLists.txt files the root never adds -- they are NOT build inputs.
CMakeLists.txt
CMakePresets.json
vcpkg.json
vcpkg-wsl.json
cmake/**
config/*
tools/packaging/*
# --- fixtures and sources the build graph names from OUTSIDE their own tree ---
# Found 2026-09-12 by tmp/scan_build_inputs.ps1 after THREE misses by eye.
#   tools/vfp/fixtures/*            src/tests/CMakeLists.txt:410 requires
#       nullfix.DBF and nullwrote.DBF and FAILS the configure without them --
#       "a lane whose only real-file proof can silently vanish has no real-file
#       proof". Globbed: the directory is 26 tracked VFP fixtures and naming two
#       is how the previous three misses happened.
#   tests/test_where_cache_only.cpp  named by src/CMakeLists.txt, needed at link.
#       NOT tests/* -- that sweeps in 65 scratch .txt files this manifest's own
#       NOT PUBLISHED section rules out.
tools/vfp/fixtures/*
tests/test_where_cache_only.cpp

# --- product edition manifests (development edition stays in dev) -----------
config/package/lean.manifest
config/package/professional.manifest
config/package/educational.manifest

# --- launchers (product front-ends: pydottalk, CLI, Workbench GUI) ----------------
#     NOT listed: holdout products (bible, erp/cascade, artic) and ALPHA
#     subsystems (pycrud, dottalk-webui).
run-pydottalk.ps1
run-cli.ps1
run-wb.ps1
run-wb-next.ps1
wb.run.ps1
wb.next.run.ps1
launch-common.ps1
tk.run.ps1
tk.run.sh

# --- engine source + headers (the WHOLE tracked set, never a subset) --------
# Subsetting is the one thing that breaks a build system. If a lane is not ready
# to publish, do not publish a slice of it -- do not commit it to development.
src/**
include/**
bindings/**

# --- runtime scaffold (structure + ini; the exe is NOT published) ----------
dottalkpp/bin/*.ini

# --- databuild / sample-build scripts --------------------------------------
dottalkpp/scripts/mcc/*.ps1
dottalkpp/data/scripts/mcc/*

